{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Prince of the land.</b> Meaning — and because of this the girl cried out, but there was none to save her." "<b>And he lay with her, etc.</b> This may be explained along the lines that the Sages of blessed memory stated (Horayot 10b) regarding the deed of Yael: that the pleasure of the wicked is suffering to the righteous. That is what the verse means by ״וַיִּשְׁכַּב אוֹתָהּ״ — even though he lay with her in the manner of a man and a woman, and by nature the woman would derive pleasure, nevertheless not only did she not derive pleasure, but on the contrary it was affliction to her. And that is what the verse means by <b>וַיְעַנֶּהָ</b>, and it was evident in her that she had no desire for him, so that he needed to speak to her heart, as it is written: ״וַיְדַבֵּר עַל לֵב״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:49.926692719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}